   "notes": "The applicable calibrant is MgO for runs 1, 3, 5, and 8 and KCl for runs 2, 4, 6, and 7, as indicated by the populated source columns. mean_temperature_k is derived exactly as (TUS+TDS)/2 because the article states that this average is the final temperature used in analysis. Parenthesized pyrometry errors are retained without assigning a confidence convention; no uncertainty is invented for the derived mean. The reported Delta-T column is transcribed verbatim even where it differs from the arithmetic difference between the rounded TUS and TDS values. The source tabulates no row-wise pressure or lattice-parameter errors.",
